&lt;p&gt;The International Tax Director will execute all aspects of international tax including compliance, transfer pricing, and planning. The International Tax Director will manage a team of tax professionals, collaborate with external advisors, and work closely with finance, legal, and business units to support global tax initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking to speak to candidates who are based in Austin, TX for our hybrid working model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support IP and tax structure planning to maximize tax efficiency&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct global tax compliance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct international quarterly and year-end accounting for income taxes (ASC 740).&amp;nbsp; Direct international tax provisions for foreign statutory financials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute the Company&#39;s global transfer pricing strategy and policy including monitoring controlled transactions, transfer prices and adjustments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and maintain intercompany agreements and allocations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review the tax components of certain customer agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review business initiatives to determine the tax impact&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct corporate international tax research and interpretation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage international tax audits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct post-acquisition integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Treasury in managing cash globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with outside tax consultants and contractors for various tax projects&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Education:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field (CPA, MST or LLM (Taxation) preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Experience:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of progressive experience in corporate tax, with at least 5 years in a leadership role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong compliance and planning experience in a multi-national, multi-entity environment including the areas of: BEAT, GILTI, FDII, Subpart F, OECD Pillar Two, Check the Box Principles, U.S. Tax Treaty Research and Interpretation, Intellectual and Intangible Property Planning, and Transfer Pricing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of international taxation in Europe and Asia&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Skills:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of SEC and GAAP reporting requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant project management skills required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to navigate complex tax issues and provide strategic solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder management abilities&lt;/li&gt;
