&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is seeking a Senior Partner Marketing Manager to build and scale high-impact go-to-market programs with strategic cloud, technology, AI, and ecosystem partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will contribute to the partner marketing strategy and execution across integrated campaigns, launches, events, digital programs, co-marketing motions, marketplace activation, and marketing enablement. Working closely with Partner team, Specialists,, Partner Strategic Operations, Alliances, Field Marketing, Global Demand Center, Product Marketing, Sales Enablement, and Communications teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Lead, Partner Marketing, the successful candidate will help drive customer adoption through partner attach and generate partner-sourced and partner-influenced pipeline, while creating repeatable programs that scale across regions and partner types.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking to speak to candidates who are based in Bengaluru for our hybrid working model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate partner capabilities, integrations, APIs, and AI solutions into compelling marketing messaging and experiences for developers, architects, IT decision-makers, executives, partner sellers, and marketers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop customer-outcome-led messaging and campaigns that clearly articulate the better together value of MongoDB plus partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute integrated, multi-channel programs leveraging the Global Demand Center and their offerings across direct, organic and paid channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support cloud marketplace, solution-listing, integration, launch, and post-launch adoption motions where applicable working closely with Cloud Partner Marketing team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create scalable marketing activation assets for partners including campaign-in-a-box kits, co-marketing plays, solution briefs, messaging guides, battlecards, demos, webinars, training, and customer-facing content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build repeatable partner marketing playbooks, content kits, and operating processes that can be localized and scaled across partners and regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead partner-facing events, executive experiences, technical webinars, workshops, and other programs that increase awareness, engagement, adoption, and demand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Marketing Operations team in improving measurement frameworks covering reach, engagement, sourced and influenced pipeline, opportunity progression, partner attach, adoption, customer acquisition, revenue contribution, and ROI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of partner/channel marketing experience in B2B technology, SaaS models, Independent Software Vendors (ISV), System Integrators and Hyperscalars&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and executing joint go-to-market plans, co-marketing programs, marketing, enablement, demand-generation campaigns, and integrated launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of product-led-growth, enterprise buyer journeys and the ability to advance the buyers journey for both technical and executive audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to simplify complex technical concepts and translate them into clear, differentiated customer and partner value propositions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with account-based marketing, co-selling, sales plays, partner referrals, or shared-account planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing budgets, MDF or co-funded investments, agencies, and multiple concurrent programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CRM, partner relationship management (PRM) platforms, marketing automation, campaign analytics, attribution, dashboards, and performance reporting, including experience supporting PRM content, resources, and partner communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to create internal enablement and external marketing content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills, attention to detail, and the ability to manage dependencies, timelines, and stakeholders across a matrixed organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A builder’s mentality, strong ownership, and comfort working in a dynamic environment where priorities and partnerships evolve quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
