&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Cool things you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In this cross‑functional role as a Technical Services Engineer, you will work with the largest and most demanding customers to drive successful implementations of MongoDB Server, MongoDB Search, and managed backups on Kubernetes platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhance your technical troubleshooting expertise and experience as a TSE (Technical Services Engineer) by working on customer use cases, evaluating solutions, customer business pain points, application architectures, and Cloud infrastructure configurations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with enterprise customers to design, implement, and troubleshoot backup strategies for massive production environments—scaling to petabytes of data—while ensuring high availability, disaster recovery readiness, and compliance with retention requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to shape the roadmap of products, tooling, and the core database by providing product feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You Need/What we are looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Patience, empathy, and a genuine desire to help others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal, with internal and external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to think on your feet, remain calm under pressure, and find solutions to challenges in real-time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong diagnostic/troubleshooting aptitude, with significant experience troubleshooting end-to-end technical issues in production environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full understanding of Linux systems and networking concepts, including firewalls, load balancers, performance tuning, storage management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience in a Support role working directly with customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience with administering RDBMSs such as Oracle, Postgres, mySQL etc. MongoDB experience is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years or more of combined experience in the following technical domains (ideally with some experience in the rest)
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in and managing Kubernetes clusters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with DevOps practices and Infrastructure-as-code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Disaster Recovery situations (Backup management, Snapshot Restores, Return-to-service operations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of mixed experience with Cloud (AWS, GCP, Azure) and on-prem infrastructure administration in a production environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI topics, development, and supporting technologies such as Vector Search&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing large-scale databases (RDBMS or NoSQL or both) and monitoring them via products like Prometheus or Grafana&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with specific MongoDB products like Ops Manager, Cloud Manager, Atlas, Kubernetes Operator/Controller&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coding in one or more of Python, Java, Go, Ruby, C, C++&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with personal test labs and reproducing issues locally to drive resolution of issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on weekends or outside of typical business hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
